{{Quote|Clockwork. He's got time powers. Speed up, slow down, forward, back.|[[Ben 10,000 (Original)|Ben 10,000]] explaining Clockwork's powers to [[Ben Tennyson (No Watch Timeline)|No Watch Ben]].<ref name="ATTWB">''[[And Then There Was Ben]]''</ref>}}
Clockwork possesses chronokinesis, which gives him the control over time itself; Clockwork can reduce the time around him, making it look as if he is moving extremely fast to bystanders.<ref name="BIM">''[[Bengeance is Mine]]''</ref> Furthermore, Clockwork can speed up and reverse time.<ref name="B10K">[[Ben 10,000 (Original)|Ben 10,000]]</ref><ref name="ATTWB" /> 

Clockwork has the ability to travel through time,<ref name="UB">[[Ben 10,000 (Ultimate Alien)|'''Ultimate Alien''' Ben 10,000]]</ref><ref name="B10KR" /> a technique that was used by Maltruant to recruit Subdora decades before his body was reconstructed in the present day.{{Refn|[[:File:Subdora Backstory.png]]|group = DJW}}

Clockwork can fire time rays from his hands or chest, which have various effects like sending people back in time,<ref name="B10KR">''[[Ben 10,000 Returns]]''</ref> manipulating the age of a person or object,<<ref name="CaFS" /><ref name="IaMMMBW1">''[[It's a Mad, Mad, Mad Ben World: Part 1]]''</ref> reversing the effects of a [[Chronosapien Time Bomb]], sending people into a [[Multiverse|different timeline]],<ref name="ATTWB">''[[And Then There Was Ben]]''</ref> and reverting them to a previous state while also immobilizing them.<ref name="IaMMMBW1" />

Clockwork possesses a degree of enhanced strength, as he was able to throw a pipe hard enough it became embedded into a wall.<ref name="BIM" /> Clockwork also possesses enhanced durability, shown when [[Looma Red Wind|Looma]] threw him at a wall at full force.<ref name="MHR">''[[Many Happy Returns]]''</ref>

Clockwork can rotate his head 360 degrees.{{Refn|[[:File:Clockwork Can Rotate His Head.png]]|group = DJW}} Additionally, by rotating the key on his head, he can create hologram-like projections of what happened in the past.<ref>''[[The Eggman Cometh]]''</ref><ref>''[[The Beginning of the End]]''</ref>

Because he is a technological being, it is possible for a [[Galvanic Mechamorph (Classic)|Galvanic Mechamorph]] to merge with Clockwork.<ref name="IaMMMBW1" />

Clockwork can still function if he loses some of his parts.<ref name="IaMMMBW1" />

==Weaknesses==
[[File:SacudidaPasado (291).png|thumb|Below Average Stamina]]
{{Quote|For a guy with time powers, he runs crazy slow!|[[Ben 23]] about Clockwork/[[Windy-Hindy|Windy-Hindy]].<ref name="IaMMMBW1"/>}}
Clockwork's time powers are completely useless in a place where there is no time at all, such as before the birth of a [[Universe (Classic)|universe]], as demonstrated with [[Maltruant]].<ref name="AND">''[[A New Dawn]]''</ref>

Clockwork's aging time rays are ineffective against anything diamond-related such as [[Petrosapien (Classic)|Petrosapiens]], since they take millions or even billions of years to age.<ref name="UB" /><ref name="B10KR" />

Clockwork can be temporarily disabled if he is exposed to a large electromagnetic pulse, such as that from a solar flare.<ref name="B10K" /><ref name="TEoaE">''[[The End of an Era]]''</ref>

The use of Clockwork's time powers creates a Sotobro effect, which is a ripple in the timestream that can be sensed or reversed by another [[Chronosapien]].<ref name="ATTWB" />

Clockwork's bulky body makes him relatively slower than other opponents and makes him an easy target for enemy attacks, as he admits that he "is not good for dodging".<ref name="BIM" /> Similarly, because of his large body and short legs, Clockwork cannot run very fast and will tire out quickly.<ref name="AJftP" />

Unlike Maltruant, Clockwork is unable to travel through dimensions, even when he is upgraded by a [[Galvanic Mechamorph (Classic)|Galvanic Mechamorph]].{{Refn|[[:File:Clockwork Cannot Travel Through Dimensions.png]]|group = DJW}}<ref name="IaMMMBW2">''[[It's a Mad, Mad, Mad Ben World: Part 2]]''</ref>

Because he is a mechanical-based being, Clockwork can be magnetized by a [[Biotsavartian]].{{Refn|[[:File:Chronosapiens Can Be Magnetized.PNG]]|group = DJW}}

Clockwork can be affected by a [[Nemuina]]'s sleeping dust.{{Refn|[[:File:Pesky Dust Works On Chronosapiens and Ectonurites.png]]|group = DJW}}

==History==
===Five Years Prior to Omniverse===
*In ''[[Ben Again]]'', 16-year-old [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] as 11-year-old Clockwork helped fix the time stream and defeat [[Eon]].

===Ultimate Alien===
*In ''[[Ben 10,000 Returns]]'', Clockwork was unlocked by [[Ben 10,000 (Ultimate Alien)|Ben 10,000]].
*Clockwork was first used by Ben off-screen prior to ''[[Inspector 13]]''.{{Refn|[[:File:Clockwork Offscreen Adventure.PNG]]|group = GT}}
*In ''Inspector 13'', [[Gwen Tennyson (Classic)|Gwen]] turned into Clockwork during a car ride to the [[Techadon Factory]].
*In ''[[Catch a Falling Star]]'', Clockwork disarmed [[Captain Nemesis]], but was caught off guard and defeated by [[Jennifer Nocturne]].
*In ''[[The Eggman Cometh]]'', Clockwork found out what happened in [[Natalie Tennyson|Natalie]]'s kitchen and realized [[Dr. Animo (Classic)|Dr. Animo]] was up to no good again.
*In ''[[The Beginning of the End]]'', Clockwork found out where the [[Flame Keepers' Circle]] had gone.

===Omniverse=== 
*In ''[[A Jolt From the Past]]'', Clockwork chased some [[Nosedeenian (Classic)|Megawhatts]] to [[Fistrick]]'s lair until he grew too tired.
*In ''[[Many Happy Returns]]'', Clockwork was defeated by [[Looma Red Wind|Princess Looma]].
*In ''[[Ben Again]]'', 11-year-old [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] as 16-year-old Clockwork helped fix the time stream and defeat [[Eon]].
*In ''[[Bengeance is Mine]]'', Clockwork defeated a [[Squid Monster]] by slowing down time.
*In ''[[And Then There Was Ben]]'', [[Ben Tennyson (No Watch Timeline)|No Watch Ben]] as Clockwork learned about his abilities from [[Ben 10,000 (Original)|Ben 10,000]]. Later, No Watch Ben as Clockwork reversed the effects of the [[Chronosapien Time Bomb]] and sent [[Albedo|Negative]] [[Ultimate Echo Echo]], [[Mad Ben]], [[Bad Ben|Bad]] [[Buzzshock (Classic)|Buzzshock]], [[Benzarro]]'s [[Frankenstrike]], [[Nega Ben]], and [[Eon]] back to their respective timelines.
* In ''[[It's a Mad, Mad, Mad Ben World: Part 1]]'', Clockwork defeated [[Mad Ben|Mad]] [[Diamondhead (Classic)|Diamondhead]] before having his powers enhanced by [[Techno-Bubble]]. He then defeated [[Exo-Skull|Exo-Skull]] and [[Subdora]] but was defeated himself by [[Maltruant]].
* In ''[[It's a Mad, Mad, Mad Ben World: Part 2]]'', Clockwork fused with Techno-Bubble again in a failed attempt to leave Mad Ben's [[Mad World|home dimension]] and return to their [[Prime Timeline|respective]] [[Dimension 23|timelines]].
*In ''[[A New Dawn]]'', Clockwork appeared for a short time as [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] was cycling through his aliens.

===[[Ultimate Alien Future Timeline|Ultimate Alien Future]]===
*In ''[[Ben 10,000 Returns]]'', [[Ultimate Ben]] used his time rays to send [[Eon]] into the past. Later, Ultimate Ben used Clockwork's time rays again in a failed attempt to destroy the [[Hands of Armageddon]] with the help of present-day [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] as [[Way Big (Classic)|Way Big]].

