==Etymology==
The term "clockwork" refers to a mechanism with a spring and toothed gearwheels, used to drive a mechanical clock and other types of devices; this refers to Clockwork being a mechanical alien with gears and time-based powers.

==Trivia==
[[File:Haywire Clockwork No Box.png|thumb|The Haywire Clockwork toy]]  
*Clockwork's appearance when he is fused with [[Techno-Bubble]] bears a strong resemblance to the [[Haywire]] Clockwork action figure, which has [[Eatle]]'s '''[[Ben 10: Ultimate Alien (TV Series)|Ultimate Alien]]''' color scheme.
*Clockwork makes gear sounds when he moves, which is similar to [[Armodrillo]] when he moves his arms.
**In '''[[Ben 10: Omniverse (TV Series)|Omniverse]]''', Clockwork ticks like a clock for the entirety of his transformation sequence, and there is a sound similar to the tolling of [[Big Ben (Classic)|Big Ben]] that sometimes appears at the end.
**The tolling clock sound also occurs when Clockwork's time rays strike their target or when he is struck on his head key.
*Clockwork speaks with a thick German accent because [[Wikipedia:Germany|Germany]] is known for inventing the watch, a portable timepiece that could tell time no matter wherever someone was in the world. Whenever Clockwork speaks in '''Omniverse''', the reverb in his voice would make a cuckoo clock sound.
*Clockwork's '''Ultimate Alien''' design, as well as 11-year-old Clockwork's design in '''Omniverse''', were created by [[Steven Choi]].{{Refn|[[:File:Steven Choi Designed UA Clockwork.png]]|group = TJC}}{{Refn|[[:File:Steven choi designed 11yo Clockwork.png]]|group = DJW}}
**Clockwork is the only alien used by 11-year-old Ben whose [[Omnitrix (Original)|Omnitrix]] symbol has a gold rim, rather than a silver one like his other aliens.
*Clockwork was originally not supposed to appear in ''[[Inspector 13]]'', with [[Heatblast (Classic)|Heatblast]] taking her role.{{Refn|[https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ben10/images/f/f1/Inspector_13_Script_DRAFT-1.pdf ''Inspector 13'' Script First Draft]|group = script|name = script1}}
*In the first draft of the script for ''[[Catch a Falling Star]]'', Clockwork bled black oil after being grievously damaged.{{Refn|[https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/ben10/images/3/3c/Catch_a_Falling_Star_DRAFT-1_October_22_2010.pdf ''Catch A Falling Star'' Script First Draft]|group = script|name = script2}}
*[[Derrick J. Wyatt]] thought that 11-year-old Ben kept Clockwork after the events of ''[[Ben Again]]'', but [[Matt Youngberg]] believed he did not.{{Refn|[[:File:Young Ben Did Not Keep Clockwork.png]]|group = DJW}}
**Concept art of 12-year old [[Kevin Levin (Classic)|Kevin's]] [[Weapon XI (Flashback)|'''Omniverse''' Flashback Mutation]] featured Clockwork's key on the sides of his head.{{Refn|[[:File:Kevin OV Mutation Prototypes 2.png]]|group = ca}}{{Refn|[[:File:Kevin OV Mutation Prototypes 3.png]]|group = ca}} However, this was removed in the final version.
*In Derrick's opinion, [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] doesn't have enough experience with Clockwork's abilities to fix [[Billy Billions (Classic)|Billy]]'s temporal condition.{{Refn|[[:File:Clockwork Can Fix Billy.png]]|group = DJW}}
*Clockwork was the final alien used by [[Ben Tennyson (No Watch Timeline)|No Watch Ben]].

